From: Claude Assistant <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jan 2025
Subject: [PATCH 0002] fftools/ffmpeg_filter: hardware acceleration detection V5

Detect hardware acceleration in filter graphs to prevent CPU scale filter
insertion in hardware-accelerated pipelines. This fixes issues where
colorspace changes would trigger unnecessary CPU scaling in NVENC/VAAPI/etc
pipelines.

Changes:
- Add uses_hwaccel flag to FilterGraphPriv
- Add filtergraph_uses_hwaccel() to detect HW frames context
- Add filtergraph_has_hw_filters() to detect HW filter names
- Skip CPU scale filter insertion for HW pipelines
- Skip colorspace format filter for HW pipelines
---
 fftools/ffmpeg_filter.c | 77 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 74 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fftools/ffmpeg_filter.c b/fftools/ffmpeg_filter.c
index 4387c99..0617882 100644
--- a/fftools/ffmpeg_filter.c
+++ b/fftools/ffmpeg_filter.c
@@ -58,6 +58,9 @@ typedef struct FilterGraphPriv {
 
     int              nb_threads;
 
+    // true when the filtergraph uses hardware acceleration
+    int              uses_hwaccel;
+
     // frame for temporarily holding output from the filtergraph
     AVFrame         *frame;
     // frame for sending output to the encoder
@@ -1679,34 +1682,48 @@ static int configure_output_video_filter(FilterGraphPriv *fgp, AVFilterGraph *gr
